Subject: [PATCH] OneWifi: configure client collectors from their typed radio policy

The client collector passed (wifi_app_t *, wifi_monitor_data_t *) to a helper
expecting (wifi_monitor_data_t *, em_config_t *). Even successful cached
provider callbacks therefore did not prove that the requested native radio
collector had been configured. Standalone link requests also lacked explicit
radio indices and a nonzero sampling interval.

Use the caller's actual policy for AP and standalone link collection. Validate
counts and mapped identities before writing monitor requests, initialize every
radio's immediate-start flag, bound VAP access/masks, and propagate admission
and configuration failures. Keep the existing AP five-second cap and standalone
ten-second sampling constant; no steering/verification deadline changes.

This fixes proven source defects, not a claim that a particular old cached
association was caused by them. Native getter/kernel membership and room
convergence still require qualification after deployment.

Upstream-Status: Pending

